Z||000000||Pike||10-15-2001||12:31 AM||||My 87 GT is really starting to come together. Thank you Chris Pond for the EGT solenoid electronic do-hicky thing-a-ma-bob and the headlight gears. No codes on the dash and life is sweet Mmmmmmm-goood! <BR>Pike<P>Black 87 GT 115K origional miles<BR>Rebuilt 2.8 (215 miles)<BR>Rebuilt C-125 Tranny<BR>Shift Kit<BR>Rebuilt Headlight gearboxes<BR>Electric Mirrors<BR>Cruise Control<BR>Electric Rear Window Defogger<BR>Electric rear deck release<BR>Factory Subwoofer performance sound<BR>10 Disk Sony CD changer<BR>Factory Sunroof<BR>OEM Sunroof shade<BR>OEM Sunroof Bag<BR>OEM Sunroof wind deflector<BR>New 450 Z series Yokahama Tires<BR>All new Switches on Dash<BR>Future: <BR>Turbo/R&E Racing, Lancaster Ca.<BR>Koni Suspension<BR>Paint Job<BR>Drivers Seat<BR>Shifter console<BR>"Life is Good"||||reg||1
Z||000001||SLYGUY||10-15-2001||12:36 AM||||Glad to hear it!!<P>Tell us a little about how you came about the rebuilt 2.8<P>What happened to the one that was in it?<BR>What did it cost you?<BR>Who did the work?<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pike||10-15-2001||12:57 AM||||<BR>Well, I did the overhaul job myself. I did a 4 banger fiero a few years ago so I decided to jump on it. I think the 2.8 was a LOT HARDER to do just because of the weight difference. I had the heads and block done at Adams metalizing, Lancaster, Ca. and they also got me a forged crank/pistons and new cam, lifters and gasket set. When I got the car the engine seemed to run OK and it even passed Kalifornia Smog, which is hard to do if the engine is bad. So I felt pretty good about it...then a few weeks after I bought it, I was on my way to work when it simply quit running. When I got the car home I did a compression test and it read Zero on No 1. So, naturally I'm thinking timeing chain, hole throught the piston...or whatever. I decided to rebuild it so that everything would be new and reliable.<BR>At this point I'm going for a total restoration. I've got the fender wells out of the rear of the car right now in order to replace the splash guards. The front of the car is very clean, In fact, I don't think the spare has ever been on the ground. I did the Armor All thing under the front hood and it all looks like new. Last night I re-conditioned my tail lights. I removed all the black guck they use to seal the lens over the shell. After a complete cleanup and polish, I used RTV to seal the lenses back in place and let them sit overnight with a weight on top...installed them this morning...they look brand new. I love the way the car handles, and in my little town of Rosamond, Ca., the GT is a real head turner...especially some of the younger kids...hell, they've never seen one before! They all think its some new Toyota or Nissan!||||reg||1
